"Sometimes, when you are sick, your body turns its own thermostat up. That is a fever. As the fever starts, 37 degrees suddenly feels too cold, so you shiver under a blanket even though your skin is hot. When the thermostat goes back to normal, you feel hot and you sweat. Your temperature also changes a little every day, even when you are well: it is lowest in the early morning and highest in the late afternoon. Keep a temperature diary with the tool below the model, and see your own daily wave.": "7e0bb0e329eb",
